omx-dsp (0.22.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * docs: keep the rendered definitions header out of the API reference
  * ci: read the package listings from a file
  * ci: a job that runs make definitions-check and make contract-dir
  * ci: the floor job reads the floor with --floor
  * ci: the RPM file list expects data/render.json
  * umbrella-separate.txt: its SPDX line
  * data: source.from links relative to the console engine's packages
    directory
  * Release 0.22.0
  * data: the import's provenance as source.from links
  * BUILDING: the definitions in data/, their rendered header and what stays
    in omx-contract
  * face-conformance: a kernel's controls from this tree only
  * definitions: the rendered header, and the code reads it
  * data: the render word for this library's own header
  * data: FBS_DEFAULT_NOTCH_Q stays with fbs.json here
  * recipes: the answers the kernel definitions were imported from
  * contract-dir: read only against a contract that dropped this tree's files
  * definitions: the hook that renders this library's own header from data/
  * data: impl links through the #define that reads an item
  * data: the DSP primitives from omx-contract 2.14.0, one file per item
  * data: eq, fbs, hrp and the continuous travels from omx-contract 2.14.0
  * contract-dir: data/ read back through omx-contract's reader
  * spdx-check: the definition files of data/ are exempt, as JSON the schema
    closes
  * face-conformance: a kernel's controls from this tree's data/kernels/ first
  * install: data/ as the package omx-dsp of the contract directory
  * data: the kernel definitions this library implements, from omx-contract
    2.14.0

